@@ -14,3 +14,7 @@
 - v1.7 adds independent transparent character layers, drag movement, Z-order and visibility management. Mouth layers switch between closed/open PNGs while dialogue is active; optional WAV voice tracks drive mouth animation for the WAV duration.
 - v1.8 removes in-game dragging for both character sprites and overlay layers. Legacy `chara` X/Y values and v1.6 save coordinates are migrated to the nearest fixed `left` / `center` / `right` anchor; layer composition coordinates remain script-defined for mouth/eye alignment.
 - Voice and layer state are persisted in the existing version-1 save container without changing the outer save schema; old saves default to an empty layer set.
+
+- v1.9 sets the native player window to a 1280×720 logical stage and persists the windowed/fullscreen preference separately from dialogue text layout. F11 / Alt+Enter toggle; Escape exits fullscreen.
+- v1.10 adds blocking visual script effects: alpha fade-in/out, darkened background crossfade, color flash and whole-stage shake. Effects use Tk after scheduling and Pillow RGBA overlays; no external runtime services are needed.
+- New visual-effect commands are included in the `.nse` validator, interpreter and `.nproj` round-trip converter. Existing commands and v1.x saves retain their previous schemas.
